# **2. Three Vertical Strategy**

Most vertical AI firms prove the model in one niche before expanding. SMB AI Ops launches across three simultaneously — not as a resource decision but a strategic one. Three independent data streams validate the GTM model in parallel. Three referral networks compound at once. Three clients by week 12 is a portfolio story that cannot be built sequentially.

## **Marine — Charter Brief**

| **Core Pain** Office managers spend 8–12 hours per week on guest communications, pre-trip coordination, and waiver routing. No AI competitor exists in this niche. FareHarbor webhook integration enables full automation from booking to guest inbox. |
| --- |

| **Element** | **Detail** |
| --- | --- |
| Free tool | Pre-trip guest brief generator — marina, date, guests, trip type → branded weather-aware email in 30 seconds |
| Primary hook | FareHarbor auto-send on booking.created — zero manual effort per booking |
| Retainer workflows | Guest comms, post-trip follow-up, review requests, DocuSign waiver routing (Q3 2026 roadmap) |
| US market | ~5,000 charter operators |
| Revenue target | $1,000–1,500/mo retainer |
| Discovery call hook | Pull up their marina live in Charter Brief, generate a real brief, ask how long this takes today |
| Key channels | Charter operator Facebook groups, marina managers, FareHarbor partner directory, NMMA, BoatUS |
| SEO targets | yacht charter guest email template, boat rental pre-trip communication, FareHarbor automation |

