# **7. Supplemental Vertical: Private AI Infrastructure**

A parallel initiative — operating independently from the three GTM verticals — validates a private GPU hosting business model targeting regulated South Florida SMBs. This is relevant to the core strategy because it directly addresses the compliance and data sovereignty concerns that make public AI tools unusable for law firms, medical practices, and financial services firms: the same regulated SMB segment that is a target for managed AI retainer services.

## **Business Case Summary — 38 Chestnut Circle PoC**

| **Thesis** The revenue opportunity is not in selling raw GPU hours. It is in selling compliance-packaged private AI infrastructure to regulated South Florida businesses who cannot safely use public AI tools. One private endpoint client at $750/month generates more net cash flow than weeks of marketplace utilization at commodity rates. |
| --- |

| **Parameter** | **Detail** |
| --- | --- |
| Phase 1 hardware | 4x RTX 4090 (24 GB VRAM each) — highest-demand consumer GPU on Vast.ai/RunPod in 2026 |
| Phase 1 CapEx | $14,350 all-in including compliance setup, legal, and insurance |
| Target clients | Law firms, medical/dental offices, financial SMBs in Broward/Miami-Dade |
| Revenue model | Private B2B endpoints ($650–2,200/mo) + marketplace spot rental (Vast.ai/RunPod) |
| CapEx breakeven | Month 4–5 with 2 pre-sold B2B clients |
| Month 18 NCF | $3,785/month net with 8 GPUs and 5 clients |
| Compliance posture | HIPAA-ready (BAA), attorney-client privilege safe via Heppner ruling defense, GLBA-aligned |
| Phase 3 vision | Miami/Doral colocation migration — 20–60 GPU deployment at $8,000–20,000/mo NCF |

**The Heppner Ruling — Strategic Sales Angle**

A February 2026 federal ruling (S.D.N.Y.) found that documents created using publicly available AI platforms are NOT protected by attorney-client privilege — because data was voluntarily disclosed to a third-party server. A private endpoint with a signed Data Processing Agreement eliminates this risk entirely. This ruling is the single most powerful sales tool for law firm outreach and applies equally to the managed AI retainer business.

**Relevance to Core Strategy**

The compliance architecture developed for the GPU hosting business — zero-retention design, VLAN isolation, TLS 1.3, HIPAA audit logging, BAA templates — translates directly into a credibility signal and sales asset for the managed AI retainer business. Clients in dental and legal verticals face the same data sovereignty concerns. The private node PoC validates a solution to the same problem.

